<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shimonoseki</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shimonoseki is a city at the south-western tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, on the Kanmon Strait facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>. Off its shore the Battle of Dan-no-ura ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genpei-war">Genpei War</a> in 1185. In 1863–64 the Chōshū domain fired on foreign ships from its batteries there, provoking Western naval bombardments, and in 1895 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-shimonoseki">Treaty of Shimonoseki</a> ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sino-japanese-war">First Sino-Japanese War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shimonoseki.jpg" alt="Shimonoseki" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wiki708 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Central_Shimonoseki_and_Kanmon_Strait.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In March 1863 the Imperial Court ordered the expulsion of the barbarians; Chōshū fired on foreign ships, beginning the <b>Shimonoseki</b> campaign, and the British bombarded Kagoshima.</blockquote><a href="/movement/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration · Course of Events</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1863 Choshu fired on foreign ships at <b>Shimonoseki</b>, moved its seat to Yamaguchi and was bombarded by Western fleets in 1864.</blockquote><a href="/state/choshu-domain">Choshu Domain</a></li></ul></section>
